  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254255/assets/7dd26869a5255376071fa5c5e2163cfb29eafddd6a2abaefbf4ec45ad3535a66.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the cosine function reaches its maximum value when $x=-2\\pi ,$ $x=0,$ and $x=2\\pi .$\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is is $x=2\\pi .$",
